WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.320
Welcome to our course on managing projects in Notion.

00:05.500 --> 00:08.320
I'm Andrea and I work on brand campaigns at Notion.

00:08.880 --> 00:12.980
A big part of my job is overseeing work across a bunch of teams,

00:13.200 --> 00:15.500
making sure stakeholders are on the same page,

00:15.960 --> 00:19.960
keeping track of project timelines and statuses so everything launches as scheduled,

00:20.360 --> 00:23.120
and keeping our brand voice consistent across channels.

00:24.040 --> 00:27.320
Managing this work in Notion ensures that everyone working on a campaign

00:27.320 --> 00:29.860
is on the same page at any point in time.

00:30.960 --> 00:35.100
In this course, you'll learn how to plan and execute a project with Notion.

00:36.440 --> 00:40.500
We'll walk you through how to set up and customize your own project management workflow

00:40.500 --> 00:43.200
in a way that's tailored to your company and team.

00:43.660 --> 00:47.900
Along the way, we'll also explore how to connect your projects to your docs in Notion,

00:48.400 --> 00:51.800
track sprints, integrate GitHub, and much more.

00:52.240 --> 00:54.900
But before getting into the details, let's zoom out.

00:54.900 --> 00:58.680
In one way or another, projects are how most of us work.

00:58.680 --> 01:01.980
They're how we turn an idea into reality.

01:01.980 --> 01:03.280
Having ideas is great.

01:03.280 --> 01:04.780
Every company has ideas.

01:04.780 --> 01:08.680
If you can't turn that idea into something real, something that is actually providing value,

01:08.680 --> 01:10.180
you will not survive as a company.

01:10.180 --> 01:16.480
Once you have an idea, you're left with the challenging task of organizing all the moving pieces of your project.

01:16.480 --> 01:18.280
Think about it.

01:18.280 --> 01:22.780
How many tasks and docs do you have to puzzle together to achieve your goal?

01:22.780 --> 01:25.280
And where does all this information live?

01:25.280 --> 01:28.580
Often, it's dozens of tools.

01:28.580 --> 01:33.580
Tasks, updates, statuses, pings, buzzes, and blips coming at you from everywhere.

01:33.580 --> 01:39.880
We believe that to do your most impactful work, project management needs to unite documentation,

01:39.880 --> 01:43.680
context, and execution in a seamless way.

01:43.680 --> 01:48.880
Old ways of running projects meant you'd have to fill these gaps with painful meetings that could have been emails,

01:48.880 --> 01:51.880
and long email threads cluttering your inbox.

01:51.880 --> 01:58.180
Instead, you can bring all your project work together in Notion for everyone.

01:58.180 --> 02:04.680
Whether your current project management system is sticky notes on your desk or a full-fledged agile workflow,

02:04.680 --> 02:07.180
Notion brings clarity and alignment.

02:07.180 --> 02:12.880
You can see the project plan, all its tasks with owners and deadlines, the meeting notes for that project,

02:12.880 --> 02:15.680
and all relevant docs in one place.

02:15.680 --> 02:20.180
In upcoming lessons, we'll focus on how you can unlock project flow state.

02:20.180 --> 02:24.180
You'll learn how to write a project plan using Notion AI,

02:24.180 --> 02:29.180
create a related project tracker with tasks and custom properties,

02:29.180 --> 02:33.180
build views of tasks for different members on your team,

02:33.180 --> 02:36.180
manage tasks in sprints,

02:36.180 --> 02:41.180
and finally, integrate your system with other essential tools, like GitHub.

02:41.180 --> 02:47.180
Enough talking. Let's dive deeper into how you can use Notion to start effectively managing your projects,

02:47.180 --> 02:50.180
starting by creating a project plan.

02:50.180 --> 02:51.180
See you soon.

